# The BigQuery plug's client side, for episode images built with
# `--warehouse-clients bigquery` (Dockerfile ALKERA_WAREHOUSE_CLIENTS): the
# Python client (AnonymousCredentials + client_options api_endpoint against
# bigquery.internal:9050, the audited proxy in front of the emulator) and the
# dbt adapter (method oauth-secrets with the box's fake token and
# api_endpoint; measured against the emulator through the proxy - debug, run,
# re-run, test and show pass; seed is a load job and is refused by name).
# dbt-bigquery pulls google-cloud-bigquery[pandas], so to_dataframe() works;
# it does NOT pull google-cloud-bigquery-storage, so the client reads results
# over REST and never dials the Storage Read API's gRPC endpoint.
# Compiled here, NOT in pyproject/uv.lock, like every backend's clients
# (docker/lock_warehouse_clients.py): constrained to the base, native and ds
# locks, so every package it shares with them is the same version; certifi is
# the one deliberate exception (bigquery-clients.overrides). Regenerate with the
# command in requirements-bigquery.lock's header.
google-cloud-bigquery[pandas]>=3.25,<4
dbt-bigquery>=1.9,<2
